From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] third_party: add riscv64 to the Azure SDK library select

The @azure alias selects a per-arch azure_library() (headers and static
libraries under /opt/<arch>-azure, /opt/<arch>-curl, ...) by target CPU,
but only has x86_64 and aarch64 branches, so any other --config fails
with "configurable attribute doesn't match this configuration".
azure_library() itself is already generic over the arch string; add the
matching config_setting and branch for riscv64 (same shape as the S3
backend's identical gap in cpp/third_party/aws.BUILD).

Upstream-Status: To upstream [this port does not open issues/PRs against third-party repos; riscv64 support in the Azure backend is exactly the kind of change upstream would want once a downstream build proves it works]
---
 cpp/third_party/azure.BUILD | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cpp/third_party/azure.BUILD b/cpp/third_party/azure.BUILD
index 518e3b5..8b8c887 100644
--- a/cpp/third_party/azure.BUILD
+++ b/cpp/third_party/azure.BUILD
@@ -23,13 +23,22 @@ config_setting(
     ],
 )

+config_setting(
+    name = "target_riscv64",
+    constraint_values = [
+        "@platforms//cpu:riscv64",
+    ],
+)
+
 azure_library(name = "azure_aarch", arch = "aarch64")
 azure_library(name = "azure_x86_64", arch = "x86_64")
+azure_library(name = "azure_riscv64", arch = "riscv64")

 alias(
     name = "azure",
     actual = select({
         ":target_x86_64": ":azure_x86_64",
         ":target_aarch64": ":azure_aarch",
+        ":target_riscv64": ":azure_riscv64",
     }),
 )
--
